{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And to El, etc.</b> The meaning: He says to the worshippers of the idol — are there in your eyes among the children of men any more honored than princes and judges? Do you not see that HaShem destroys them in an instant?" "<b>and I will compare.</b> That I may compare with Him:" "And the meaning of <b>holy</b> is that HaShem is holy from being compared to any of His works, even to a work of His works."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:13.243872156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}